From: Matteo Bruni <mbruni@codeweavers.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dsound: Flush denormals in the mixing thread.

Backport of WineHQ commit 1f8afa945a (wine-11.3, Matteo Bruni).

Denormal floats are far slower than normal ones. 64-bit processes
default to flushing them, but 32-bit processes do not, so the
resampling and mixing of a 32-bit application could fall behind the
mixer period and underrun, which is heard as stutter and crackle.

--- a/dlls/dsound/mixer.c
+++ b/dlls/dsound/mixer.c
@@ -760,8 +760,10 @@
 DWORD CALLBACK DSOUND_mixthread(void *p)
 {
 	DirectSoundDevice *dev = p;
+
 	TRACE("(%p)\n", dev);
 	SetThreadDescription(GetCurrentThread(), L"wine_dsound_mixer");
+        _controlfp_s(NULL, _DN_FLUSH, _MCW_DN);
 
 	while (dev->ref) {
 		DWORD ret;
